  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Socioeconomic Integration of Migrants and Vulnerable  Persons of Host Communities in Colombia - Puentes de Inclusi&#xf3;n</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;The Action &#xbf;&lt;strong&gt;Socioeconomic Integration of Migrants and vulnerable persons of host communities in Colombia &#xbf; &lt;em&gt;Puentes de Inclusi&#xf3;n&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&#xbf; is jointly co-financed by the European Union and the Federal Ministry for Economic Cooperation and Development (BMZ), and implemented by GIZ as part of the BMZ program &#xbf;Supporting Host Communities for Refugees and Migrants in the Border Regions of Colombia, Ecuador and Peru (SI FRONTERA)&#xbf;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;The duration of this Action is scheduled from January 01&lt;sup&gt;st&lt;/sup&gt;, 2025 to September 30&lt;sup&gt;th&lt;/sup&gt;, 2027 (33 months, excluding the closing phase of 3 additional months) with a total budget of 7.0 Mio. EUR (EU contribution 6.0 Mio. EUR and BMZ contribution 1.0 Mio. EUR). BMZ&#xbf;s total funding for the project &#xbf;Supporting Host Communities for Refugees and Migrants in the Border Regions of Colombia, Ecuador and Peru (SI FRONTERA)&#xbf; in Colombia is 21.56 Mio.EUR.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;The Action is part of and contributes to the Team Europe Initiative Peace Colombia, to which France, Germany, Ireland, Italy, the Netherlands, Portugal, Spain, Sweden and KfW contribute. The Team Europe&#xbf;s contribution to migration is around EUR 150 million. The Action also contributes to the BMZ&#xbf;s &#xbf;Special initiative Refugees and Host Countries&#xbf; (&lt;em&gt;Sonderinitiative &#xbf;Gefl&#xfc;chtete und Aufnahmel&#xe4;nder&#xbf;&lt;/em&gt;).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;The Action aims to strengthen the socioeconomic integration of migrants and vulnerable locals in Colombia to promote social cohesion while maintaining peace and economic growth (&lt;strong&gt;Overall Objective&lt;/strong&gt;).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;This Action &#xbf;&lt;strong&gt;Socioeconomic Integration of Migrants and vulnerable persons of host comunities in Colombia&lt;/strong&gt;&quot; consists of:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;a. a budget support component directly managed by the European Union&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;b.an indirect management component carried out by &lt;em&gt;Deutsche Gesellschaft f&#xfc;r Internationale Zusammenarbeit&lt;/em&gt; (GIZ) GmbH. This Description of the Action (DoA) refers to the indirect management component.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;The &lt;strong&gt;Specific Objective&lt;/strong&gt; (Outcome) of the indirect management component of the Action is formulated as follows: improved opportunities for sustainable integration of migrants and members of host communities into local economies with an intersectional approach.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;The &lt;strong&gt;Areas of Support&lt;/strong&gt; (Outputs) of the Action are aim for the following:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: black;&quot;&gt;Job opportunities have been generated in cooperation with the public and private sector to promote gender-responsive labour market inclusion, using an intersectional approach to reach those facing the greatest barriers to integration &lt;/span&gt;(&lt;strong&gt;Output 1&lt;/strong&gt;).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;Migrants and vulnerable members of host communities have improved their skills for employment and self-employment, using an intersectional approach (&lt;strong&gt;Output 2&lt;/strong&gt;).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;Equal participation and leadership of local institutions and community-based organizations are strengthened (&lt;strong&gt;Output 3&lt;/strong&gt;).&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
